# Docs Clarity Review Checklist

Full scored report: `evals/DOCS_CLARITY_EVALUATION.md`. Human process: `CONTRIBUTING.md` (Documentation Pull Requests).

## Integrity gates

- [ ] **Release sync:** version bumps update `docs/install/getting_swcdb/` download table, `swc.install.archive` default, and `SWCDB_VERSION=` examples together
- [ ] **Link check:** new/changed relative links under `docs/` resolve (especially `use/thriftclient/*`)
- [ ] **TOC sync:** new `docs/**/README.md` with `title:` → intro TOC line, sidebar-only note, or `nav_exclude: true` for redirects
- [ ] **Code↔docs:** changes to Comparators / Thrift `Comp`, CMake options, or `src/etc/swcdb` defaults update matching docs in the same PR

## Page hygiene

- [ ] Keep YAML frontmatter (`title`, `sort`)
- [ ] Prefer factual integrity (versions, broken links, TOC gaps) over drive-by rewrites
- [ ] Section hubs list children with one-line purpose (not stub-only)
- [ ] Redirect stubs: `nav_exclude: true` so sidebar shows one canonical entry
- [ ] Canonical OS-tuning path is `docs/configure/os_tuning/` (`os_tunning/` is redirect-only)

## Mirrors (when mentioning published docs)

- www.swcdb.org — latest **release** docs
- GitHub Pages (`kashirin-alex.github.io/swc-db`) — current **master**
- ReadTheDocs — additional mirror

## Remaining known gaps (do not invent as fixed)

- Source `0.5.13` vs packages `0.5.12` until next package release
- Thin CLI admin shells; optional automated link-check CI still open
